I'm reading through the lojban reference grammer found here:
http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-download_wiki_attachment.php?attId=196&page=The+Lojban+Reference+Grammar
but it's annoying me that the text is showing up misaligned for some
reason.  eg.

6.2)  mi        ti           [cu] vecnu ta
    --        --                ===== --
    seller-x1 goods-sold-x2     sells buyer-x3
    I         this              sell  to that.

    (translates as stilted or poetic English)
    I this thing do sell to that buyer.

Is it just showing up this way in my browser or is it like this for anyone
else as well?  It seems like the lojban text word-wraps where it shouldn't
and that the "-"s and "="s are offset by a few characters.

 - LB

